{"changes":["cmd/plugin.go: two-tier classification (registry = official, --repo = third-party), --repo/--yes flags, consent decision point (injectable runner.consent, production pluginConsentPrompt: non-TTY refuses, TTY prompts via ui.Select defaulting to abort), renderThirdPartyInfo (Source URL + Summary + Capabilities), inspectStaged (staged-manifest smoke check before finalize, returns the manifest), Trust row in the install header and summary","cmd/plugin_lifecycle.go: update --yes flag; named third-party update resolves the repo from the installed manifest source (repoFromInstalled/parsePluginSource) and applies the consent flow; staged inspection moved before the atomic .old swap (the smoke-check-failure restore path is gone); Trust row in the update header; update --all still official-only","plugin/registry.go: doc comment updated to the implemented two-tier model (name-in-registry = official)","cmd/plugin_test.go / cmd/plugin_lifecycle_test.go: run/runUpdate signature updates, help-contract updates, refusal-message updates"],"role":"implementation","summary":"Implemented the two-tier plugin trust model (sto:plugin-trust-model). Registry-listed (maleolabs) plugin names install without a prompt (official, full-trust); every other source is third-party and requires explicit consent after its source and capabilities are surfaced. Added `--repo \u003cowner/name\u003e` to `eka plugin install` (third-party by definition — the registry is bypassed) and `--yes` to install/update for non-interactive consent. Consent timing (design decision): download + checksum verification + staged-manifest inspection happen FIRST (fail-closed, both tiers), then the third-party source/capabilities are shown and consent is asked BEFORE finalize; declining removes the staged download and refuses (exit 1). A non-terminal run without --yes refuses with the --yes hint — the CLI never auto-consents silently. The staged binary's manifest is now inspected before anything moves into place (p